<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 61,004 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 61,004 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 61,004 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday compared to 120,555 tonnes in the same period on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Monday	Feb 23</p>
<p>    Export cargo		18,207	14,471</p>
<p>    Import cargo		42,797     106,084</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, six ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, four are expected to sail and eight are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>High speed diesel    56,000	 Al-Maqwa	     24/2</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 60,000	 Al-Safa		24/2</p>
<p>Palm oil		 16,500	 Bunga Cenderewasih 28/2</p>
<p>Containers		  400	 Energy		 28/2</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
